.TH "jaro" "1" "" "" ""
.SH jaro(1)
.SS Name
jaro \- command line interface for Jaromail workflows
.SS Synopsis
\f[CR]jaro [options] [command] [command\-options]\f[R]
.SS Description
\f[CR]jaro\f[R] is the operational CLI for Jaromail.
It orchestrates account configuration, local maildir operations,
addressbooks, filtering, indexing and SMTP/IMAP actions.
.SS Options
\f[CR]\-a ACCOUNT\f[R] use a specific account instead of
\f[CR]default\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]\-l LIST\f[R] use a specific addressbook/list (default:
\f[CR]whitelist\f[R]).
.PP
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] dry\-run mode where supported.
.PP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R] quiet mode.
.PP
\f[CR]\-D\f[R] debug mode.
.PP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R] show help.
.PP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R] or \f[CR]\-\-version\f[R] prints the assigned release
version and exits.
The startup banner and help use the same installed metadata.
Source builds derive it from release tags, with the v6.0.0 development
baseline when no v6 tag exists.
.PP
\f[CR]\-f\f[R] force mode for selected operations.
.SS Filter engine selection
\f[CR]JARO_FILTER_ENGINE=legacy|native\f[R] selects compilation and
filter/fetch dispatch; unset selects native.
Explicit \f[CR]JARO_FILTER_ENGINE=legacy\f[R] selects rollback.
Empty/unknown values fail.
Native \f[CR]update\f[R]/\f[CR]sieve\f[R] invoke the installed compiler
with explicit mail/account roots and return its failures without
fallback.
No profile file is required: built\-in defaults enable fileinto,
automatic mailbox creation and the qualified legacy ERE subset.
Regex is declared only when used; partial addresses keep matching
without wildcard suffixes.
Unsupported ERE exports fail with a source\-line diagnostic.
Explicit legacy rejects typed/domain records.
Sieve generation writes the local export only, without remote
deployment.
.PP
Native \f[CR]filter [MAILDIR]\f[R] compiles/verifies once and applies
one pinned batch.
The default Maildir is \f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/incoming\f[R].
Native \f[CR]fetch\f[R] uses the same batch after transport and
refreshes the index once, even after partial failure; batch errors
remain nonzero.
Filter itself does not index.
Native Sieve import accepts the bounded Jaromail\-generated grammar
described below.
.PP
Fresh \f[CR]init\f[R] under unset/explicit native installs a
comment\-only typed\-example policy with builtins active.
Explicit legacy keeps the original 14 ERE defaults.
Existing policies are never replaced or translated.
Supported legacy EREs need no profile configuration; patterns outside
the qualified subset need a deliberate rewrite.
\f[CR]save\f[R] and \f[CR]move\f[R] are aliases.
Invalid selectors or missing required templates fail before bootstrap
configuration writes.
.PP
Native \f[CR]filter \-\-explain [MAILDIR]\f[R] and
\f[CR]\-n filter [MAILDIR]\f[R] classify only, checking the selected
generation against current policy without publishing.
Missing/stale generations return 5 and request an explicit
\f[CR]jaro update\f[R].
Native \f[CR]\-n fetch\f[R] explains local incoming mail without
transport or indexing.
.PP
Native \f[CR]filter \-\-compare FILE [MAILDIR]\f[R] compares retained
actual final legacy observations against native classification.
It never applies either engine.
FILE uses complete fingerprint\-bound JLC1 NUL framing described in
\f[CR]filter\-interfaces.md\f[R].
Its producer must retain unchanged\-corpus hashes and actual legacy
provenance.
Ambiguous dry\-run proposals and unsupported files fail; this command
does not infer a legacy winner from proposal text.
.SS Commands
.SS Core mail flow
\f[CR]doctor [\-\-json]\f[R] report local setup problems without
initialization, network requests, credential retrieval or repair.
\f[CR]jaro \-a ACCOUNT doctor\f[R] checks a selected account.
It continues through independently discoverable problems even if mail
tools or version metadata are missing.
Exit status is 0 when there are no blocking findings, 1 for actionable
blockers, and 2 for invalid invocation or an internal diagnostic
failure.
Human output suggests commands without running them.
\f[CR]\-\-json\f[R] emits schema version 1 with stable check IDs,
status, redacted \f[CR]explanation\f[R] and \f[CR]next_action\f[R]
strings, resolved paths and \f[CR]exit_status\f[R].
Warnings and unknown checks do not make the exit status nonzero.
See the manual\[cq]s offline diagnostics section for the complete schema
and setup flow.
.PP
\f[CR]wizard\f[R] interactive account setup.
.PP
\f[CR]fetch\f[R] fetch unread messages for an account.
.PP
\f[CR]send\f[R] send queued messages from \f[CR]outbox/\f[R].
.PP
\f[CR]outbox list\f[R] print stable queue IDs, delivery states and
classified outcomes without message content or recipients.
This route does not initialize files, consult credentials or require the
mail transport tools.
.PP
\f[CR]outbox retry ID \-\-confirm\-duplicate\f[R] explicitly retry only
a held uncertain item.
The required flag acknowledges possible duplicate delivery.
\f[CR]\-a ACCOUNT\f[R] selects its account.
A new uncertain result is held again.
.PP
\f[CR]outbox archive ID\f[R] record externally verified delivery and
complete the local sent copy without SMTP or account/credential access.
Accepted, verified and complete items can also finish local recovery
this way.
.PP
Both actions accept \f[CR]\-n\f[R] for validation without writes or
transport.
Unknown, stale, ambiguous and content\-mismatched IDs are refused.
See delivery recovery for states, examples and damaged\-state handling.
Bare \f[CR]outbox\f[R] still opens the outbox Maildir in Mutt.
.PP
\f[CR]queue\f[R] read a full message from stdin and queue it.
.PP
\f[CR]smtp\f[R] read a full message from stdin and send via SMTP.
.PP
\f[CR]peek\f[R] open remote IMAP mailbox view.
.PP
\f[CR]open\f[R] open a local maildir folder.
.SS Recipient groups
Local recipient lists live in \f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/Groups/\f[R] (for
example \f[CR]Mail/Groups/team\f[R]) and are addressed as
\f[CR]team\[at]jaromail.group\f[R].
The first line may set \f[CR]#mode individual\f[R],
\f[CR]#mode cc\f[R]/\f[CR]#mode carboncopy\f[R], or
\f[CR]#mode bcc\f[R]; when no \f[CR]#mode\f[R] is set, groups use
\f[CR]#mode individual\f[R].
.SS Account and secrets
\f[CR]passwd\f[R] set or update account password in the configured
keyring.
.PP
\f[CR]askpass\f[R] print account password resolved from keyring/prompt.
.PP
\f[CR]isonline\f[R] check network reachability.
.SS Search and indexing
\f[CR]index\f[R] update the search index.
.PP
\f[CR]search\f[R] run search queries over local mail archives.
.PP
\f[CR]header\f[R], \f[CR]headers\f[R] print mail headers.
.SS Addressbook and contacts
\f[CR]abook\f[R] edit addressbook.
.PP
\f[CR]addr\f[R], \f[CR]list\f[R] list addresses from addressbook.
.PP
\f[CR]extract\f[R], \f[CR]parse\f[R] extract addresses from supported
inputs.
.PP
\f[CR]import\f[R] import addresses from stdin.
.PP
\f[CR]export\f[R] export addresses to another format.
.PP
\f[CR]learn\f[R], \f[CR]isknown\f[R], \f[CR]complete\f[R] contact
learning/query/completion helpers.
.SS Filtering and Sieve
\f[CR]update\f[R] rebuild local filtering cache and regenerate Sieve.
.PP
\f[CR]filter\f[R] apply filters to a maildir.
.PP
\f[CR]sieve\f[R] regenerate \f[CR]Filters.sieve\f[R] only.
.PP
\f[CR]sieve\-import FILE\f[R] import a Jaromail\-generated Sieve file
into local filter/addressbook files.
With \f[CR]JARO_FILTER_ENGINE=native\f[R], the bounded token parser
validates and stages the complete import before publication.
\f[CR]\-n\f[R] validates without writes;
\f[CR]\-\-legacy\-generated\f[R] explicitly recovers older generated
header\-contains scripts with a migration diagnostic.
Arbitrary provider scripts are unsupported.
See the import contract for supported grammar, profile/mapping
requirements and recovery behavior.
.SS Maildir and utility commands
\f[CR]backup\f[R] move search results between maildirs.
.PP
\f[CR]merge\f[R] merge one maildir into another.
.PP
\f[CR]deliver\f[R] deliver a message from stdin into a maildir.
.PP
\f[CR]rmdupes\f[R] remove duplicate messages.
.PP
\f[CR]remember\f[R], \f[CR]replay\f[R], \f[CR]preview\f[R],
\f[CR]edit\f[R], \f[CR]vim\f[R], \f[CR]imap\f[R], \f[CR]alot\f[R],
\f[CR]alot\-config\f[R], \f[CR]notmuch\f[R], \f[CR]notmuch\-config\f[R],
\f[CR]isml\f[R], \f[CR]ismd\f[R].
.SS Files
\f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR\f[R] mail root (default usually
\f[CR]$HOME/Mail\f[R]).
.PP
\f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/Accounts/\f[R] account configuration files.
.PP
\f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/Groups/\f[R] local recipient group files.
.PP
\f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/Filters.txt\f[R] filtering rules.
.PP
\f[CR]$JAROMAILDIR/Filters.sieve\f[R] generated Sieve rules.
.SS See Also
\f[CR]jaromail(1)\f[R]
